      "title": "Scene 2: Depth of Field",
      "place": "City Hall Park fountain, Broadway & Murray St",
      "body": "Background artists never run; they drift across the frame so the director can establish depth. The park has served as a civic stage since George Washington heard the Declaration read aloud here.",
      "move": "Walk the rim of the fountain counterclockwise at half your normal pace. Let two hurried strangers cut in front of you without reacting.",
